The '''Guadalquivir''' ({{Literally|the great river}}; {{Langx|kp|Paraná-Ipi'i|4=strong waterway}}) is a [[W:Strait|strait]] on the [[Levante, Balisca|east coast]] of [[Atlántida]], and the main channel from which [[Salto Bay]] empties into the [[W:Atlantic Ocean|Atlantic Ocean]]. It is defined by the [[W:Promontory|promontory]] of the [[Umuarama Peninsula]] and [[Itacajá Point]]. The entire western shoreline and adjacent waters throughout the strait are included in the [[Guadalquivir Ecological Reserve]].

